                <pb facs="0195" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 772/251.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Jay to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-07-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                    1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Jay reports that he has been informed by the vice minister for foreign
                    affairs that the time and place of meeting of the opium commission are agreeable
                    to the Japanese Government, and that the appointment of commissioners is
                    awaiting action by the new cabinet. States that as the method of investigation
                    must be referred to the Government of Formosa, some delay is unavoidable.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
